<title>UK: Donaldson Lufkin to buy UK's Phoenix Group.</title>
<headline>Donaldson Lufkin to buy UK's Phoenix Group.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. investment bank Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette said Tuesday it would buy British financial advisory firm  Phoenix Group Ltd for an undisclosed amount.  </p>
<p>The new group, called DLJ Phoenix, would play a leading role in developing DLJ's investment banking business in Europe and Asia, the firms said in a joint statement.</p>
<p>Martin Smith, a founding partner of Phoenix, will serve as chairman of DLJ Phoenix.</p>
<p>All of Phoenix's directors and staff will remain with the new organisation, the companies said.</p>
